PROVENANCE - tb/base2001.7z
===========================

base2001.7z is an overlay for tb/base.7z: 33 precompiled inputs in the object
format the 2001 port emits - big-endian ELF, e_machine 0x7262, symbol case as
written in the source. base.7z ships the same 33 paths in the format the current
port emits - little-endian ELF, e_machine 0x1051, symbols uppercased by the
assembler. `make check DATA_OVERLAY=.../base2001.7z` unpacks base.7z and then
this archive over it, so the 2.11.2 toolchain links inputs it can read.

A 34th file, lib/www51.sc, rides along because the linker script names one of
those symbols; section 6 says what was done to it and why.

What a run with this overlay produces, and how it compares to the reference
ROMs base.7z ships: frozen-report.md.

Archive sha256: 03399d746b3909d471548fefc7b4f3b66341c32521c2d5d4133e7f27bdf3ea13
Archive size:   27907 bytes


------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SINGLE SOURCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Every file comes from ONE place - the 2001 testbench archive, git blob

  mcs51-2.11.2-original:gnu13.tar.gz

in the backup mirror L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/backup/binutils-mcs51.git
(blob size 132303 bytes). Retrieval, read-only:

  git fetch --depth=1 L:/ai/binutils-mcs51/backup/binutils-mcs51.git \
      mcs51-2.11.2-original
  git cat-file blob FETCH_HEAD:gnu13.tar.gz > gnu13.tar.gz
  tar xzf gnu13.tar.gz

Files are copied out of gnu13/lib and gnu13/cgi byte-for-byte. No conversion,
no repacking, no re-assembly: the tarball already holds them in the old format,
which is what the 2001 toolchain reads.

precompiled_gnu114.rar was NOT used. It is a 2002-09-15 snapshot, a year later
than gnu13; its libk80.a is 48912 bytes against gnu13's 42638, and
tb/objects-report/REPORT.md shows it is missing modules (http, makeipreply,
smtp, udpchecksum in libk80.a; mul2x2, fsearch, fsend, eewrite in libw80.a)
that both gnu13 and the current base.7z contain. gnu13 supplies all 33 files
the overlay needs, including web51_80.obj and web51_23.obj, so nothing has to
be filled in from the rar.


